# macOS
.DS_Store

# Dependencies — teammates run `npm install` themselves
node_modules/

# ── Secrets (belt-and-braces: also ignored by per-folder .gitignore) ──
# Google OAuth for the google-sheets MCP — each user creates their own
MCP-configurations/mcp-sheets/credentials.json
MCP-configurations/mcp-sheets/token.json
# Grafana service-account token
MCP-configurations/grafana/.token
# Redmine (tracker.example.com) API key
MCP-configurations/redmine/.token
# Mega.nz account credentials
MCP-configurations/mega/credentials.json
# Test-account pools hold passwords (users.json is credentials by convention, everywhere;
# the old 'Load-Testing/**' prefix was orphaned by the 12/07 folder regroup and left
# non-template users.json trackable — made location-proof 28/07/2026)
**/users.json
# Usage browser-scraper Chrome profile — holds live claude.ai session cookies
Claude-Extra-Skills-Features/Usage/usage-scraper/profile/

# Logs & local artifacts
*.log
# Self-healing locators rubric configs carry real stand creds (Loop-Engineering kit);
# canonical location is <Project>/UI-Automation/rubric.config.json OUTSIDE this repo,
# but ignore everywhere as belt-and-braces
**/rubric.config.json
**/rubric-baseline/
**/rubric-verdicts/
# PageSpeed Insights API key (free, per-user — never shared)
MCP-configurations/pagespeed/.token
# Memory-Eval gate state — local, per-machine, never shippable. `.warned/` filenames are LIVE chat
# session ids; `.last-green` is a hash of YOUR memory file and can never match a teammate's.
# Default state dir is the script's own folder (override: EVAL_GATE_STATE_DIR), i.e. inside this
# repo — so these must be ignored for the unattended `git add -A` backup to stay safe.
Claude-Extra-Skills-Features/Memory-Eval/.last-green
Claude-Extra-Skills-Features/Memory-Eval/.warned/
# A REAL scenario set and any run result are authored about the user's OWN config: their situations and
# oracles carry exactly the nouns (clients, hosts, ids) that must never ship, and a result quotes the
# measured memory file verbatim. So everything .json here is ignored by default and the shipped example is
# the single explicit exception — fail-closed: a new example must be un-ignored deliberately, whereas a
# forgotten pattern would silently track someone's data. SETUP tells the user to copy the example into this
# very directory, so this is the landing spot, not a hypothetical.
Claude-Extra-Skills-Features/Memory-Eval/*.json
!Claude-Extra-Skills-Features/Memory-Eval/scenarios.example.json
Claude-Extra-Skills-Features/Memory-Eval/runs/
